  "notes": [
    "Independent public-data sidecar only. No portfolio, ledger, signal, leverage or execution setting is modified.",
    "Yahoo futures use explicit WTI/NQ December 2026 and Brent January 2027 symbols; no continuous futures and no automatic roll. A conservative review cutoff is not a claimed expiration timestamp.",
    "Yahoo regularMarketTime is the provider quote observation time. Reception delay is visible in freshness.age_ms; no claim of real-time exchange entitlement is made.",
    "provider_previous_close is only a same-instrument provider reference, never a common 30-minute return across markets.",
    "Official bond feeds expose dates, not actual observation/publication times. They remain date-only diagnostics and cannot satisfy intraday risk admission.",
    "Euro yields use one public Radiocor daily benchmark brief with explicit GMT observation time. These are provider generic benchmarks, not executable prices; all derived euro spreads require the same report snapshot.",
    "Daily sources have independent six-hour polling clocks. HTTP 403/429 are not bypassed; at least one hour of backoff applies.",
    "Session labels are finite reference diagnostics only; closed, maintenance or unknown sessions cannot admit intraday observations. They never renew quote age.",
    "Session reference expires November 2 New York midnight; expired or unreviewed dates become unknown until independently maintained.",
    "Daily observations remain ineligible for intraday use even when their source gives an explicit GMT observation minute.",
    "Transient transport timeouts use bounded retry backoff; successful daily reads retain six-hour polling. Identity/parse failures do not receive fast retries and HTTP denial backoff is preserved."
  ],
